  "notes": "FORMS:\n{寝|ね} (sleep) + {落|お}ちる (to fall) → to fall into sleep\n{寝落|ねお}ちする (to fall asleep unintentionally)\n\nMODERN USAGE:\nThis term became popular with the rise of smartphones and online communication. It's commonly used when:\n- Falling asleep while texting or on social media\n- Dozing off during an online video call\n- Falling asleep while gaming\n\nUSAGE:\n- LINEで{話|はな}していて{寝落|ねお}ちした (fell asleep while chatting on LINE)\n- {通話|つうわ}{中|ちゅう}に{寝落|ねお}ち (falling asleep during a call)\n- ゲーム{中|ちゅう}に{寝落|ねお}ち (falling asleep while gaming)\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- うたた{寝|ね} (dozing off lightly)\n- {居眠|いねむ}り (nodding off while sitting)\n- {仮眠|かみん} (intentional nap)",
